Chipotle’s board of directors has approved a $1.8 billion share buyback program, increasing the company’s total remaining buyback capacity to approximately $1.85 billion as of Dec. 5.&nbsp;

The move represents a strategic shift in Chipotle’s capital-return strategy, transitioning from quarterly buyback authorizations to larger sums designed to span multiple quarters.&nbsp;

